Step-by-Step Setup Guide - 2026

Follow these steps to build and configure the shortcut on macOS or iOS. Refer to images for clarity.


Prerequisites

Open Apple Reminders and create a target list (e.g., Shop).

Inside your list, create a dedicated reminder item named Total (or create a section/subcategory header titled Total).

Step 1: Build the Shortcut Workflow

Open the Shortcuts app and create a new shortcut named Shopping Total.


Add the following actions in exact order:

1. Fetch Shopping Items

Add Action: Find Reminders

Filter Rules:

List is Shop

Is Not Completed

Title does not contain Total

Set Sort by to None and leave Limit unchecked.

2. Extract Prices

Add Action: Match Text

Pattern: \d+(\.\d{2})?

Input: Reminders (Output from Step 1)

3. Calculate the Sum

Add Action: Calculate Statistics

Operation: Sum

Input: Matches (Output from Step 2)

4. Find the Target "Total" Item

Add Action: Find Reminders

Filter Rules:

List is Shop

Title contains Total

Set Sort by to None and check Limit to 1.

5. Update the Header Title

Add Action: Set Title

Target: Reminders (Output from Step 4)

Text to set: Total : $ + Sum (Output from Step 3)

Step 2: Configure Automatic Triggers

To ensure the shortcut runs hands-free without opening the Shortcuts app every time:


Option A: Run Automatically on App Close (Recommended)

Open Shortcuts $\rightarrow$ Navigate to the Automation tab.

Tap + and select App.

Set App to Reminders and check Is Closed.

Select Run Immediately (disable Ask Before Running).

Set the action to Run Shortcut and choose Shopping Total.


Option B: Hardware Back Tap Trigger

Go to System Settings / Settings $\rightarrow$ Accessibility $\rightarrow$ Touch $\rightarrow$ Back Tap.

Assign Double Tap or Triple Tap to the Shopping Total shortcut.

Double-tap the back of your device while viewing your list to update the sum on screen instantly.

Usage Syntax Guidelines

Format items in your Reminders list with prices attached at the end or within the title text:

Granola bars — $3.97

Tomato — $1

Ghee — $11

The Regular Expression automatically extracts all valid numeric formats ($3.97, $1, $11) and aggregates the result under your list's Total heading.
